WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.056
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.326 --> 00:08.718
I don't have the confidence

3
00:08.718 --> 00:10.842
to be a good person to someone.

4
00:10.842 --> 00:14.774
I'm bad at expressing myself, and I'm emotionally numb.

5
00:14.774 --> 00:18.986
So chances are... I'll disappoint you a lot.

6
00:18.986 --> 00:21.850
If you're okay with that...

7
00:21.850 --> 00:23.610
I'm in!

8
00:24.418 --> 00:26.202
Let's do it!

9
00:26.202 --> 00:27.358
Friends!

10
00:27.358 --> 00:30.028
Friends?

11
00:36.962 --> 00:39.872
- FWB! - Clear the way!

12
00:39.872 --> 00:41.546
- Out of the way! - Cardiac arrest!

13
00:41.546 --> 00:43.670
- Cardiac arrest! - Please move!

14
00:43.670 --> 00:45.614
Let us pass!

15
00:45.614 --> 00:49.042
- What? - Friends with benefits!

16
00:49.042 --> 00:51.016
Oh, you're awake.

17
00:51.016 --> 00:52.946
Fortunately, there are no broken bones.

18
00:52.946 --> 00:55.754
It's just a light sprain, so don't overdo it. You can go.

19
00:55.754 --> 00:58.254
- Well, excuse me, Doctor! - Yes?

20
00:58.254 --> 01:00.874
By any chance, did you scan her head too?

21
01:00.874 --> 01:03.060
Her head? It looked fine.

22
01:03.060 --> 01:04.562
Why, are you feeling uncomfortable?

23
01:04.562 --> 01:06.832
No, I'm perfectly fine.

24
01:08.215 --> 01:09.858
I'll pretend I didn't hear that.

25
01:09.858 --> 01:13.038
[Episode 8] I'm telling you, it's not a good idea.

26
01:13.038 --> 01:16.802
We're just trying to see each other without any pressure.

27
01:16.802 --> 01:19.536
I am feeling pressure.

28
01:20.330 --> 01:22.498
Why?

29
01:22.498 --> 01:25.751
Am I really that unattractive?

30
01:27.178 --> 01:30.534
Seriously, do you even know what FWB means when you say that?

31
01:30.534 --> 01:33.986
I know that much.

32
01:33.986 --> 01:37.806
It's a relationship where you mutually exchange just what's physically necessary.

33
01:37.806 --> 01:38.810
I know.

34
01:38.810 --> 01:40.562
A relationship with no interference, jealousy,

35
01:40.562 --> 01:42.674
or emotional communion whatsoever.

36
01:42.674 --> 01:44.010
I said that I know.

37
01:44.010 --> 01:47.894
Whether I meet, sleep with, or date another woman other than you,

38
01:47.894 --> 01:49.498
you have no right to get mad.

39
01:49.498 --> 01:51.850
I said I know!

40
01:51.850 --> 01:54.638
Gong Nam Su! Aren't you coming?

41
02:08.414 --> 02:10.194
Hold on.

42
02:11.362 --> 02:13.402
Dr. Park Chang Su, attending physician.

43
02:13.402 --> 02:15.110
Bruised while working out.

44
02:15.110 --> 02:18.345
X-rays clear, I just tripped.

45
02:19.090 --> 02:20.886
Perfect!

46
02:20.886 --> 02:22.898
Let's ditch the crutches.

47
02:22.898 --> 02:24.413
Probably for the best, right?

48
02:27.705 --> 02:28.734
Oh, right, Yeon Su!

49
02:28.734 --> 02:30.634
What?

50
02:30.634 --> 02:34.594
I'll tell them about that myself, so keep your mouth shut, okay?

51
02:34.594 --> 02:37.922
Fine, understood.

52
02:37.922 --> 02:40.498
If you're done plotting, head inside.

53
02:40.498 --> 02:41.806
The elders will worry.

54
02:41.806 --> 02:45.402
Okay, Mr. Dokgo. Thanks for the ride.

55
02:45.402 --> 02:47.674
And...

56
02:47.674 --> 02:50.358
I'm going to talk to Si Eun a bit more...

57
02:50.358 --> 02:52.238
Right...

58
02:53.138 --> 02:56.382
- Okay. - What's with you two?

59
02:56.382 --> 02:59.737
- Wait, you knew? - Well...

60
02:59.737 --> 03:01.882
I told him.

61
03:02.717 --> 03:06.610
Why would you tell Mr. Dokgo Dal? I'm your sister.

62
03:06.610 --> 03:08.826
I just...

63
03:08.826 --> 03:11.398
wanted to talk to an adult man.

64
03:16.534 --> 03:19.330
Let's talk tomorrow at work.

65
03:19.330 --> 03:21.110
Work?

66
03:22.138 --> 03:24.578
Wait, you two work at the same company?

67
03:24.578 --> 03:26.746
Then, you work at an adult toy company too?

68
03:26.746 --> 03:27.842
- No, I don't. - She was dispatched.

69
03:27.842 --> 03:29.864
Totally out of sync!

70
03:29.864 --> 03:31.318
I'm just on dispatch...

71
03:31.318 --> 03:33.648
No way! Gong Yeon Su, you're crazy!

72
03:33.648 --> 03:35.922
That actually puts my mind at ease.

73
03:37.275 --> 03:39.360
Hey, you watch your mouth too!

74
03:39.360 --> 03:41.357
Don't worry!

75
03:42.061 --> 03:43.890
I haven't done this in ages.

76
03:44.522 --> 03:46.975
Ancestors!

77
03:52.866 --> 03:55.901
An... Ancestors.

78
03:56.538 --> 04:00.274
- Ancestors? - We swear to keep the secret before them.

79
04:00.274 --> 04:02.386
What are you waiting for? Put your hand on top.

80
04:02.386 --> 04:04.466
What?

81
04:04.466 --> 04:07.838
- Me too? - You know two of our secrets.

82
04:07.838 --> 04:10.270
Who on earth would I tell them to?

83
04:10.270 --> 04:13.182
You just blabbed earlier.

84
04:13.182 --> 04:15.166
No needless words, just swear it!

85
04:15.166 --> 04:18.126
They're not even my ancestors, they're total strangers' spirits...

86
04:18.126 --> 04:20.092
Just do it already.

87
04:22.750 --> 04:24.863
An... Ancestors!

88
04:26.042 --> 04:28.058
Okay!

89
04:34.002 --> 04:36.525
Oh, dear! What happened to you?

90
04:36.525 --> 04:39.021
How were you playing basketball?

91
04:39.021 --> 04:41.122
There's not a single uninjured spot on you?

92
04:41.122 --> 04:44.541
Messing around so carelessly with an exam coming up... Goodness!

93
04:44.541 --> 04:47.170
Are you taking the exam with your body?

94
04:47.170 --> 04:49.994
As long as his head is fine, that's what matters. Poor thing...

95
04:49.994 --> 04:53.398
My precious eldest grandson...

96
04:53.398 --> 04:55.598
How did you hurt yourself?

97
04:55.598 --> 04:58.978
I fell! I slipped getting off the bus...

98
04:58.978 --> 05:02.538
You should've been careful.

99
05:02.538 --> 05:05.662
If you had a husband to drive you around, would this have happened?

100
05:05.662 --> 05:09.634
Dad, is Nam Su's leg a pillar while Yeon Su's is firewood?

101
05:09.634 --> 05:12.333
Why blame only Yeon Su?

102
05:13.510 --> 05:15.750
I should just propose to anyone on the street.

103
05:15.750 --> 05:17.388
Don't rebel by gambling with your life.

104
05:17.388 --> 05:20.434
- That's how I ended up divorced. - Stop bickering and just go inside.

105
05:20.434 --> 05:23.974
Besides, this is nothing! You know when I was little?

106
05:23.974 --> 05:27.546
My brother, I mean, your dad fell, and I fell into a poop-pit, huh?

107
05:27.546 --> 05:28.966
Do you remember that, Dad?

108
05:28.966 --> 05:30.606
You helped my brother up first,

109
05:30.606 --> 05:31.746
and only rescued me after that!

110
05:31.746 --> 05:34.391
I broke out in rashes all over from the sewage,

111
05:34.391 --> 05:36.650
and had to rub soybean paste all the way to my fingertips!

112
05:36.650 --> 05:39.918
Mom, that paste you made, I had to smear it everywhere!

113
05:39.918 --> 05:41.806
- Remember that? Seriously? - Good grief!

114
05:41.806 --> 05:44.761
Stop bringing that up! Go inside already! Oh, my goodness!

115
05:44.761 --> 05:46.855
- I can bring it up for three more years... - In this family

116
05:46.855 --> 05:48.948
where sons are pillars and daughters are firewood,

117
05:48.948 --> 05:53.166
my aunt rebelled dramatically through marriage and divorce.

118
05:53.166 --> 05:55.112
And I...

119
06:07.334 --> 06:11.661
I broke the mold silently in a different way.

120
06:20.522 --> 06:24.516
[The Psychology of Men Who Want FWB: Why?]

121
06:29.413 --> 06:31.224
[Opportunistic thinking: Craving sex without responsibility!]

122
06:31.224 --> 06:36.587
[Self-defense mechanism: Straddling between friendship and sex!]

123
06:36.587 --> 06:40.098
[Rules are essential for the relationship!]

124
08:11.150 --> 08:13.386
Should I bring out more fresh kimchi?

125
08:13.386 --> 08:15.926
- Do you want more fresh kimchi? - I'm good.

126
08:15.926 --> 08:19.874
Come on, you need to eat well to heal faster.

127
08:19.874 --> 08:24.038
Yeon Su, why don't you bring Yoon Jio home one more time?

128
08:25.858 --> 08:28.830
What? Why him all of a sudden?

129
08:28.830 --> 08:30.474
So we can play Go together.

130
08:31.789 --> 08:35.074
Grandpa, why would you play Go with him?

131
08:35.074 --> 08:38.518
Then, do you want to go on a blind date?

132
08:38.518 --> 08:40.694
Grandpa!

133
08:40.694 --> 08:45.734
What good is bringing two men home if nothing comes of it?

134
08:45.734 --> 08:47.821
No matter how much rice is in the pantry,

135
08:47.821 --> 08:50.698
you'll starve if you don't cook it!

136
08:50.698 --> 08:54.534
So is that why you're cooking it for her, Dad?

137
08:54.534 --> 08:56.898
But why Yoon Jio of all people?

138
08:56.898 --> 08:59.294
Yeon Su needs to have at least one child.

139
08:59.294 --> 09:00.954
And for that, she needs someone to plant the seed.

140
09:00.954 --> 09:03.833
Stop complaining and bring him over.

141
09:05.638 --> 09:10.290
Please, Grandpa, I'll take care of it myself.

142
09:10.290 --> 09:12.578
Will you take care of it after I'm in my coffin?

143
09:12.578 --> 09:15.553
Enough. Don't talk back anymore.

144
09:22.718 --> 09:24.604
I can't bring him.

145
09:25.626 --> 09:27.607
What did you say?

146
09:30.110 --> 09:32.109
He's just a coworker.

147
09:32.109 --> 09:34.738
There's no reason for him to visit our house.

148
09:34.738 --> 09:38.243
I'm late for work, so I'll get going.

149
09:40.106 --> 09:42.055
Hey, hold on!

150
09:47.603 --> 09:48.670
Thank you for the meal.

151
09:48.670 --> 09:50.765
Why not eat more?

152
09:50.765 --> 09:52.570
I'm also full.

153
09:52.570 --> 09:54.326
Goodness, look at him...

154
09:54.326 --> 09:58.894
Dad, turning thirty next year means she's still in her prime.

155
09:58.894 --> 10:03.382
Honestly, I'm the one in a rush, not her!

156
10:03.382 --> 10:07.426
- Isn't there any decent divorcee for me? - You!

157
10:07.426 --> 10:11.550
One kid would be nice, though it's too late for me to give birth now.

158
10:11.550 --> 10:14.430
Gosh, if I'd known, I would've frozen my eggs.

159
10:14.430 --> 10:15.906
- Jeez... - Mi Young.

160
10:15.906 --> 10:17.362
Didn't you say you were going to the mineral spring?

161
10:17.362 --> 10:19.742
Me? The spring...

162
10:19.742 --> 10:22.509
Right, I did! Wow, I totally did!

163
10:22.509 --> 10:24.723
Thanks!

164
10:24.723 --> 10:26.870
Here's some scorched rice water.

165
10:26.870 --> 10:29.709
Oh, gosh.

166
10:31.166 --> 10:32.726
Oh, dear...

167
10:32.726 --> 10:33.941
- Oh, no... - You...

168
10:33.941 --> 10:36.941
- This is... Ouch! - Oh, dear...

169
10:39.826 --> 10:45.185
I seriously wish I could just marry out and leave...

170
10:50.346 --> 10:52.890
Aren't you going to be late if you're leaving just now?

171
10:52.890 --> 10:56.750
Wait, why are you here at this hour?

172
10:56.750 --> 10:58.540
How are you feeling?

173
11:01.082 --> 11:05.914
Don't tell me you came to pick me up?

174
11:06.882 --> 11:11.486
Well, you got hurt because of me, carpooling is the least I can do.

175
11:11.486 --> 11:13.755
Besides, it's on my way...

176
11:17.934 --> 11:19.734
Let's go.

177
11:30.742 --> 11:36.986
Wait, do friends with benefits usually pick each other up like this?

178
11:38.166 --> 11:40.762
Well, we're friends.

179
11:40.762 --> 11:42.722
And this is the benefit?

180
11:44.093 --> 11:45.787
The benefit.

181
12:24.550 --> 12:25.798
[Two Months Pregnant]

182
12:25.798 --> 12:29.172
[Morning sickness begins]

183
12:30.086 --> 12:33.714
Ah, no wonder. Morning sickness must be worse by now.

184
12:33.714 --> 12:35.503
Nam Su.

185
12:36.722 --> 12:40.433
Nam Su!

186
12:41.398 --> 12:44.113
Why are you coming out of there?

187
12:44.113 --> 12:46.598
Oh, I came to borrow this.

188
12:51.954 --> 12:54.306
Nam Su.

189
12:54.306 --> 12:55.958
Yeah?

190
12:55.958 --> 13:00.403
Is someone in this house dating?

191
13:04.178 --> 13:05.741
Your sister, I mean.

192
13:07.842 --> 13:10.906
Why flip your sentence structure like that, Mom? You scared me!

193
13:10.906 --> 13:14.978
I saw her getting in some guy's car in front of the house just now.

194
13:14.978 --> 13:17.934
Really? I don't know.

195
13:17.934 --> 13:19.486
- You really don't know? - I don't.

196
13:19.486 --> 13:20.570
Ask her yourself.

197
13:20.570 --> 13:22.398
Is that so?

198
13:24.894 --> 13:27.386
Clean your room once in a while.

199
13:27.386 --> 13:29.006
Mom.

200
13:29.006 --> 13:30.866
What?

201
13:31.538 --> 13:34.374
- Back when you were pregnant with me... - Yeah?

202
13:34.374 --> 13:37.194
Did you have morning sickness too?

203
13:37.194 --> 13:40.402
Where is this coming from all of a sudden?

204
13:40.402 --> 13:42.366
Just curious.

205
13:42.366 --> 13:45.293
It was better than when I had your sister,

206
13:45.293 --> 13:48.386
but it was pretty bad with you too.

207
13:48.386 --> 13:50.234
Is it... really tough?

208
13:50.234 --> 13:54.499
Don't even ask! It felt like being seasick all day long.

209
13:55.418 --> 14:00.346
I barely survived on the plum extract your grandmother made.

210
14:00.346 --> 14:04.954
Strangely enough, that was the only thing that settled my stomach.

211
14:04.954 --> 14:06.770
Plum extract?

212
14:06.770 --> 14:08.710
Do we have any at home?

213
14:08.710 --> 14:10.514
We do. Want some?

214
14:10.514 --> 14:12.746
No, later...

215
14:12.746 --> 14:14.510
What?

216
14:15.526 --> 14:16.834
Is your stomach upset?

217
14:16.834 --> 14:19.494
No, no, I'm fine.

218
14:19.494 --> 14:20.526
Hurry up and go to the academy.

219
14:20.526 --> 14:22.485
- Okay. - Yeah.

220
14:26.386 --> 14:28.124
Plum extract.

221
14:35.914 --> 14:37.675
Here.

222
14:38.562 --> 14:41.162
What's this?

223
14:41.162 --> 14:43.138
A bagel shop opened nearby.

224
14:43.138 --> 14:44.822
You bought it for me?

225
14:44.822 --> 14:48.762
I bought it for myself, but it was buy-one-get-one-free.

226
14:50.365 --> 14:55.506
I usually prefer rice for breakfast,

227
14:55.506 --> 14:57.418
but I'll enjoy it.

228
14:57.418 --> 14:59.334
The one marked there is the latte.

229
14:59.334 --> 15:01.482
Oh, latte! Sweet!

230
15:12.826 --> 15:17.154
I gave it some thought yesterday.

231
15:17.154 --> 15:18.893
About what?

232
15:19.562 --> 15:22.486
Twice a week. No more than that.

233
15:22.486 --> 15:24.380
Twice?

234
15:25.418 --> 15:27.374
Why?

235
15:27.374 --> 15:31.804
Is that... too little?

236
15:40.934 --> 15:44.326
Then... three times? But every other week.

237
15:44.326 --> 15:46.086
Every other week?

238
15:48.218 --> 15:51.021
And no motels.

239
15:51.021 --> 15:53.242
I'd rather do it at home.

240
15:54.962 --> 15:56.790
Excuse me.

241
15:56.790 --> 15:58.018
Yes?

242
15:58.018 --> 15:59.999
Just eat the bagel.

243
16:01.186 --> 16:03.074
Okay...

244
16:07.610 --> 16:10.566
Also, too bright is a bit much.

245
16:10.566 --> 16:15.562
I know you hate the dark, Mr. Dokgo Dal,

246
16:15.562 --> 16:19.650
but if it's too bright, it's embarrassing.

247
16:19.650 --> 16:22.563
A single lampshade light is fine.

248
16:26.414 --> 16:28.690
What did you write there? Let me see.

249
16:28.690 --> 16:30.634
No, you can't!

250
16:30.634 --> 16:32.082
- Is there more? - Huh? No, not at all!

251
16:32.082 --> 16:34.370
- Give it to me. - No, no way!

252
16:34.370 --> 16:37.578
That's all of it. I'm done. Thank you for the food!

253
16:38.482 --> 16:39.766
Can I take it away?

254
16:39.766 --> 16:41.550
Just eat it.

255
16:43.778 --> 16:44.779
[Hello. I'm inquiring again regarding product purchases.]

256
16:44.779 --> 16:46.406
[I looked into all the women's and couples' products you recommended...]

257
16:46.406 --> 16:49.826
[Hello, Munch. This is Loand...] Man, he sure has a lot of questions.

258
16:49.826 --> 16:52.193
Buy something first before asking.

259
16:54.862 --> 16:56.445
What's the problem?

260
16:57.501 --> 17:00.582
He said he wanted to get a gift for his wife, so I recommended a bunch,

261
17:00.582 --> 17:02.462
but he doesn't have the courage to actually give it to her.

262
17:02.462 --> 17:04.429
I recommended couple products,

263
17:04.429 --> 17:07.398
but he says it's just a lease, so they don't even dare use it.

264
17:07.398 --> 17:09.346
What does he want me to do?

265
17:10.014 --> 17:11.698
You said he's a new customer, right?

266
17:11.698 --> 17:14.630
He just inquired about men's products a moment ago.

267
17:14.630 --> 17:16.994
What's the point of explaining everything?

268
17:16.994 --> 17:18.764
He hasn't bought anything for months.

269
17:18.764 --> 17:21.798
Just keeps asking the same over and over.

270
17:21.798 --> 17:23.066
Am I an answering machine?

271
17:23.066 --> 17:25.618
Since it's his first time, he must be nervous.

272
17:25.618 --> 17:29.714
His inner desires and guilt are probably at war.

273
17:31.214 --> 17:33.414
- His username is Munch, right? - Yes.

274
17:33.414 --> 17:37.394
Last time, he asked if we could package it in a prostate supplement box.

275
17:37.394 --> 17:40.318
He said his family must never find out. He's pretty creative.

276
17:40.318 --> 17:42.146
So, did you do it?

277
17:42.146 --> 17:44.082
How could I do it when he never bought it?

278
17:44.838 --> 17:48.922
How about giving him points or coupons?

279
17:48.922 --> 17:54.346
Right! Don't give them to guys like Peter Panty, give them to Munch!

280
17:54.346 --> 17:56.102
I should bring that up at the meeting.

281
17:56.102 --> 17:57.686
What about the performance report? Did you hand it over?

282
17:57.686 --> 18:01.522
Yeah. JC Investment's reaction was better than expected.

283
18:01.522 --> 18:04.457
They're even talking about an offline store.

284
18:06.430 --> 18:09.058
Did you talk to Ms. Yeon Su?

285
18:10.826 --> 18:13.007
- What did she say? - Just...

286
18:14.410 --> 18:16.719
that we should get along.

287
18:19.482 --> 18:22.098
Excuse me, not between you two.

288
18:22.098 --> 18:27.730
Does our marketer seem likely to stay on good terms with our company?

289
18:30.294 --> 18:34.326
Well, probably?

290
18:54.626 --> 18:57.702
I'll do my own laundry!

291
18:57.702 --> 19:00.738
It'll get wrinkled, just leave it.

292
19:00.738 --> 19:02.562
Stop doing the kids' laundry too.

293
19:02.562 --> 19:04.094
I like doing it.

294
19:04.094 --> 19:07.269
You're really something!

295
19:43.482 --> 19:45.182
Goodness...

296
19:57.666 --> 20:01.657
What's going on? What is it...

297
20:08.934 --> 20:10.226
What is this?

298
20:10.226 --> 20:14.242
Encyclopedia of Pregnancy, Childbirth, and Childcare?

299
20:14.242 --> 20:16.742
I found it in Yeon Su's room.

300
20:16.742 --> 20:19.400
What do you think this means?

301
20:20.830 --> 20:24.382
Th-This... is...

302
20:24.382 --> 20:26.649
Why would she have this?

303
20:27.538 --> 20:33.290
Oh, she probably needs it for work reference, right?

304
20:33.290 --> 20:37.154
Yeon Su has all sorts of books in her room!

305
20:37.154 --> 20:41.738
Last time, I even saw that book, "The Humanities of Poop"!

306
20:41.738 --> 20:46.346
I didn't find it on the bookshelf, but under her bed.

307
20:46.346 --> 20:51.048
Well, that's... because she didn't want people to get the wrong idea...

308
20:55.922 --> 20:57.590
Even after seeing this?

309
20:57.590 --> 20:59.970
Wh-What's this?

310
21:03.162 --> 21:05.947
Oh, my gosh... She's lost her mind!

311
21:05.947 --> 21:09.798
Is Yeon Su pregnant?

312
21:09.798 --> 21:11.952
Keep your voice down!

313
21:14.258 --> 21:16.270
She went on a rampage unboxing this.

314
21:16.270 --> 21:18.594
I knew it would come to this! I really did!

315
21:18.594 --> 21:20.666
Yeon Su has a man.

316
21:20.666 --> 21:22.882
Seeing him pick her up in front of the house this morning,

317
21:22.882 --> 21:24.906
they can't just be casual.

318
21:24.906 --> 21:28.362
Then it's not Candidate Number One, it's Number Two!

319
21:28.362 --> 21:30.214
Number Two? If it's Number Two...

320
21:30.214 --> 21:34.078
Yoon Jio! Don't you remember?

321
21:34.078 --> 21:38.730
They said Dokgo Dal has azoospermia!

322
21:38.730 --> 21:40.190
What are we going to do?

323
21:40.190 --> 21:42.432
Oh dear, this is an emergency! What do we...

324
21:42.432 --> 21:47.655
What are you going to do about this?

325
21:48.862 --> 21:51.133
We have to find out the truth first.

326
21:53.090 --> 21:55.938
I'm so full. I ate too much!

327
21:59.174 --> 22:01.582
Should we bet coffee on that?

328
22:01.582 --> 22:04.046
Ladies sit back, only men step up.

329
22:04.046 --> 22:06.910
Why, looking for a way to use your muscles?

330
22:06.910 --> 22:11.374
Come on, you'll get hurt. This is surprisingly heavy.

331
22:11.374 --> 22:14.142
Shall we give it a shot? Just for fun!

332
22:14.142 --> 22:16.606
Forget it. I'll buy the coffee.

333
22:16.606 --> 22:20.830
True. My kick might be weaker than yours, but my punch is stronger.

334
22:20.830 --> 22:23.090
Looks like you'll have to buy it anyway.

335
22:28.226 --> 22:32.516
All right, I'll go first!

336
22:39.101 --> 22:41.659
830?

337
22:47.430 --> 22:49.046
Look at you, not bad!

338
22:50.733 --> 22:53.326
Mr. Yoon! That's really strong.

339
22:53.326 --> 22:56.346
You were great at batting last time too.

340
22:56.346 --> 22:59.277
Ah, my rotational power is good.

341
22:59.277 --> 23:01.666
I was super close

342
23:01.666 --> 23:03.718
with the baseball team in high school.

343
23:05.085 --> 23:06.614
Oh, three tries?

344
23:06.614 --> 23:08.746
Min Hyeong, you hit the last one too.

345
23:08.746 --> 23:10.518
Should I?

346
23:18.658 --> 23:20.405
Are you going to hit it?

347
23:22.418 --> 23:24.846
You must be confused. My kick is stronger,

348
23:24.846 --> 23:26.796
and my punch is stronger too.

349
23:26.796 --> 23:30.950
You were only better than me at claw machines, remember?

350
23:45.315 --> 23:48.026
Practice and try again!

351
23:48.026 --> 23:50.653
Oh, I'm suddenly getting a call.

352
23:50.653 --> 23:52.206
Um, hello?

353
23:52.206 --> 23:57.693
I'll go get the coffee!

354
23:58.514 --> 24:00.813
Wait, I'll come with you!

355
24:03.174 --> 24:07.046
Did you see that? Ms. Yeon Su smiled.

356
24:07.046 --> 24:09.863
Hey, let's settle this.

357
24:14.122 --> 24:15.242
Did you ask her out?

358
24:15.242 --> 24:17.942
Are we kids? Asking out loud to start dating?

359
24:17.942 --> 24:20.450
If you don't say it, how do you confirm the feelings?

360
24:20.450 --> 24:23.544
Why? Are you curious?

361
24:25.490 --> 24:28.433
Not really! I know your pattern all too well.

362
24:28.433 --> 24:31.149
But Ms. Yeon Su doesn't know, though.

363
24:31.149 --> 24:33.406
Should I tell her?

364
24:33.406 --> 24:37.830
Even if her heart is with you, her family's heart is with me.

365
24:37.830 --> 24:39.901
You have no idea how much her grandfather adores me.

366
24:39.901 --> 24:42.997
Have you ever had the stewed hen her mother made?

367
24:42.997 --> 24:44.934
- What? - I have.

368
24:44.934 --> 24:46.668
Hey! That's foul play! Come on!

369
24:46.668 --> 24:48.770
That's technique.

370
24:52.048 --> 24:53.490
- One more time! - Just admit it.

371
24:53.490 --> 24:54.502
You lost.

372
24:54.502 --> 24:57.402
Then let's do the claw machine! The claw machine!

373
24:57.402 --> 24:59.906
What are you doing here?

374
24:59.906 --> 25:02.683
Are you two playing games?

375
25:04.810 --> 25:07.588
Stop that and come outside.

376
25:09.530 --> 25:11.425
Hey, wait for me!

377
25:13.626 --> 25:15.574
I'm heading out first!

378
25:15.574 --> 25:17.102
Are you going home?

379
25:17.102 --> 25:20.122
For once, my husband wants to eat out.

380
25:20.122 --> 25:24.586
We're going for all-you-can-eat shabu-shabu. See you tomorrow!

381
25:24.586 --> 25:27.174
I'll get going too!

382
25:27.174 --> 25:28.866
Who are you flirting with tonight?

383
25:28.866 --> 25:31.805
A sexy lady who buys me good food.

384
25:31.805 --> 25:33.521
Fighting!

385
25:41.334 --> 25:43.478
Guess I should get going too.

386
25:43.478 --> 25:45.518
You're leaving already, Mr. Yoon?

387
25:45.518 --> 25:49.421
I have dinner plans. See you tomorrow!

388
25:51.100 --> 25:53.443
[How to make pasta]

389
25:53.443 --> 25:55.754
[Becoming a sexy guy who cooks] A sexy guy who cooks...

390
25:55.754 --> 25:58.331
[Home date! Easy and simple Aglio e Olio]

391
26:00.918 --> 26:03.327
Aglio e Olio?

392
26:13.686 --> 26:19.258
Mr. Dal, I was about to head home...

393
26:19.258 --> 26:21.428
Let's grab dinner.

394
26:23.018 --> 26:24.790
At my place.

395
26:38.826 --> 26:39.934
Care for a game of Go?

396
26:39.934 --> 26:42.854
What Go?

397
26:42.854 --> 26:43.938
Five-in-a-row?

398
26:43.938 --> 26:45.566
No, thanks.

399
26:45.566 --> 26:47.396
Flicking stones?

400
26:54.166 --> 26:56.486
Do you know how to play Go?

401
26:56.486 --> 26:59.950
I only know how to place the stones!

402
26:59.950 --> 27:01.818
- Put it in. - Is he asking for his number?

403
27:01.818 --> 27:04.366
- Pardon? - Put your number in.

404
27:04.366 --> 27:06.055
- Oh, yes, sir! - No, you can't!

405
27:06.055 --> 27:08.542
It's fine, he won't call.

406
27:09.750 --> 27:11.598
Come over next time for a match.

407
27:11.598 --> 27:13.322
Just call me, and I'll come running!

408
27:13.322 --> 27:14.557
Alright.

409
27:26.962 --> 27:29.438
Well, feeding you counts as dinner plans too.

410
27:39.154 --> 27:40.954
Hello?

411
27:42.786 --> 27:44.754
Oh, yes!

412
27:47.434 --> 27:49.173
[In Use]

413
27:55.202 --> 27:59.494
Hey, Ms. Gong. What's up?

414
27:59.494 --> 28:01.750
Whoa, slow down a bit!

415
28:01.750 --> 28:03.990
Is it finally game time?

416
28:03.990 --> 28:06.975
That's not what's important!

417
28:07.930 --> 28:09.010
I...

418
28:09.010 --> 28:11.462
Yeah, what?

419
28:11.462 --> 28:14.074
Today,

420
28:14.074 --> 28:16.862
my underwear doesn't match!

421
28:16.862 --> 28:17.870
And?

422
28:17.870 --> 28:20.214
Top and bottom don't match at all!

423
28:20.214 --> 28:22.717
Different colors, different fabrics!

424
28:24.094 --> 28:27.266
Should I just tell him to do it next time?

425
28:27.266 --> 28:31.334
You're taking them off anyway, who cares if it's mismatched or rags?

426
28:31.334 --> 28:35.074
Still... it feels wrong!

427
28:35.074 --> 28:37.689
If I saved all the money I spent on lingerie,

428
28:37.689 --> 28:40.234
I could've opened an underwear boutique in Gangnam.

429
28:40.234 --> 28:43.153
It's all pointless, you know?

430
28:43.770 --> 28:45.626
Sera!

431
28:47.498 --> 28:50.522
So don't worry and just do it! I'm hanging up.

432
28:50.522 --> 28:53.090
Wait! Wait, listen!

433
28:53.090 --> 28:54.690
Aw, so cute!

434
28:54.690 --> 28:56.798
Seriously!

435
29:05.254 --> 29:07.134
Right.

436
29:07.134 --> 29:10.362
Instead of stripping piece by piece,

437
29:10.362 --> 29:11.558
let's take it all off at once.

438
29:11.558 --> 29:15.354
Yeah, that works! It'll be fine.

439
29:15.354 --> 29:17.022
Quickly...

440
29:17.022 --> 29:20.982
Yeah. I'll just get it over with in one go.

441
29:23.778 --> 29:26.680
- Hello? - Get what over with?

442
29:28.438 --> 29:30.802
Oh, Mom!

443
29:30.802 --> 29:33.341
Overtime... I meant...

444
29:33.341 --> 29:35.926
getting my work done in one shot...

445
29:35.926 --> 29:37.542
Do you have to work overtime today?

446
29:37.542 --> 29:39.818
Yeah... I really want to...

447
29:41.306 --> 29:43.662
I mean, I have to. Why?

448
29:43.662 --> 29:46.450
Never mind. We'll talk when you get home.

449
29:49.074 --> 29:50.787
What was that about?

450
29:54.922 --> 29:57.410
She says she's working overtime and will be late.

451
29:57.410 --> 30:00.278
Why does she always do this at times like this?

452
30:00.278 --> 30:02.834
Baek Hee, do we have any makgeolli left?

453
30:02.834 --> 30:05.170
Oh, yes! Are you feeling peckish?

454
30:05.170 --> 30:07.246
You just had dinner not long ago.

455
30:07.246 --> 30:09.514
Serve it later with some cabbage pancakes.

456
30:09.514 --> 30:11.966
- Later? - I have a guest coming over.

457
30:11.966 --> 30:13.714
Oh, yes!

458
30:28.834 --> 30:30.586
To be honest,

459
30:30.586 --> 30:33.010
I thought I'd have to take the stairs again,

460
30:33.010 --> 30:35.226
so I was secretly worried.

461
30:39.490 --> 30:44.430
Still, since I've been here once, it feels familiar.

462
30:44.430 --> 30:48.518
I really have no idea what he's thinking.

463
30:48.518 --> 30:52.646
Sauté the garlic in olive oil... Wait, there's no garlic!

464
30:52.646 --> 30:58.018
He wouldn't just jump right into it the moment we get here, right?

465
30:58.018 --> 31:01.149
They probably won't deliver a single bag of garlic.

466
31:01.818 --> 31:03.819
Should I go buy some?

467
31:11.318 --> 31:13.036
Wait...

468
31:14.262 --> 31:15.426
Where's the bathroom?

469
31:15.426 --> 31:17.894
Oh, over there.

470
31:56.102 --> 31:57.886
- Ms. Gong Yeon Su. - Yes?

471
31:57.886 --> 31:59.806
I'll step out for a moment. It won't take long.

472
32:01.229 --> 32:03.837
Okay, see you soon.

473
32:14.066 --> 32:17.100
Still, this isn't right. Why am I here?

474
32:18.186 --> 32:20.222
But, how could I turn down an elder's invitation?

475
32:20.222 --> 32:23.246
He even called me directly.

476
32:23.246 --> 32:26.909
Oh, you're here!

477
32:28.090 --> 32:30.670
Baek Hee! Our guest is here!

478
32:30.670 --> 32:31.674
Hello, sir!

479
32:31.674 --> 32:33.658
Welcome. Have you eaten?

480
32:33.658 --> 32:36.330
- Not yet, sir! - All right, come on in!

481
32:40.826 --> 32:44.158
This is truly a feast.

482
32:44.158 --> 32:47.394
You said you haven't eaten. Go ahead and dig in.

483
32:47.394 --> 32:50.222
Yes, eat plenty.

484
32:50.222 --> 32:53.487
- Thank you for the meal. - Of course!

485
32:56.514 --> 33:00.874
Seeing you rush over the moment Father called

486
33:00.874 --> 33:04.430
means you must be quite close with Yeon Su.

487
33:04.430 --> 33:09.558
I'm here today as his Go buddy, not as Yeon Su's friend.

488
33:09.558 --> 33:12.402
Trying to win over the elders first, are we?

489
33:12.402 --> 33:15.742
Come by more often. Your feet need to get used to our threshold

490
33:15.742 --> 33:17.566
if you're going to join the family, don't you think?

491
33:17.566 --> 33:20.830
Oh, the family?

492
33:21.602 --> 33:24.309
If only that could happen, that would be wonderful.

493
33:25.190 --> 33:28.446
- The more I look, the better he seems. - Indeed!

494
33:28.446 --> 33:32.302
Does Yeon Su know you're here, Mr. Yoon?

495
33:32.302 --> 33:35.571
I haven't told her yet.

496
33:35.571 --> 33:40.358
Stop interrogating him and let him eat in peace.

497
33:40.358 --> 33:44.058
Eat up, round two is cabbage pancakes and makgeolli!

498
33:44.058 --> 33:45.806
Yes, sir!

499
33:46.478 --> 33:48.142
He has no idea, does he?

500
33:48.142 --> 33:51.069
Here, have some fish too.

501
34:01.710 --> 34:03.006
Who is it?

502
34:03.006 --> 34:04.234
Delivery!

503
34:04.234 --> 34:06.394
What?

504
34:06.394 --> 34:09.087
Si Eun, it's me.

505
34:14.542 --> 34:15.554
Nam Su?

506
34:15.554 --> 34:17.853
Why didn't you answer when you were home?

507
34:17.853 --> 34:20.014
I was worried.

508
34:20.014 --> 34:23.326
Eat this. There were so many orders for these dumplings,

509
34:23.326 --> 34:25.085
so I bought some for you too.

510
34:26.061 --> 34:27.814
And here.

511
34:27.814 --> 34:31.192
It's plum extract. They say it helps with an upset stomach.

512
34:35.974 --> 34:37.782
What are you doing

513
34:38.534 --> 34:40.590
- right now? - Working my part-time job!

514
34:42.778 --> 34:46.298
My leg felt better than I thought,

515
34:46.298 --> 34:48.251
so eat everything you want

516
34:49.674 --> 34:51.671
until next week.

517
34:59.262 --> 35:01.422
Si Eun!

518
35:01.422 --> 35:03.790
Your choice is my choice.

519
35:03.790 --> 35:07.145
I'll take full responsibility, okay?

520
35:07.802 --> 35:10.426
So don't worry about anything.

521
35:12.822 --> 35:15.786
Heat up the dumplings before you eat them!

522
35:18.994 --> 35:20.822
Why...

523
35:21.822 --> 35:24.888
Why do you always make me the bad guy?

524
35:53.666 --> 35:56.820
Maybe just one glass...

525
36:45.138 --> 36:48.163
Oh, wait...

526
37:14.874 --> 37:18.182
I pressed the wrong button...

527
37:18.182 --> 37:20.361
What do I do?

528
37:49.462 --> 37:50.670
Just leave it.

529
37:50.670 --> 37:52.642
It's a preset for the lighting I usually use.

530
37:52.642 --> 37:54.850
Ah... lighting...

531
37:54.850 --> 37:57.065
Would you like a glass of wine?

532
37:57.810 --> 37:59.926
You're already having one.

533
37:59.926 --> 38:03.446
I was... thirsty...

534
38:04.082 --> 38:06.830
How about some simple pasta for dinner?

535
38:06.830 --> 38:09.654
Are you good at cooking?

536
38:09.654 --> 38:13.218
Well... somewhat?

537
38:13.218 --> 38:17.198
So this is?

538
38:17.198 --> 38:19.278
Aglio... e Olio...

539
38:19.278 --> 38:22.310
Yes, Aglio e Olio.

540
38:25.646 --> 38:29.948
No vampire would dare come close.

541
38:30.938 --> 38:32.951
That's an interesting review.

542
38:37.306 --> 38:41.842
Is it really that inedible?

543
38:44.462 --> 38:46.746
You haven't cooked much, have you?

544
38:46.746 --> 38:50.342
Actually, the first dish I made after moving here

545
38:50.342 --> 38:53.658
was the cheonggukjang your mother gave me.

546
38:53.658 --> 38:55.506
What?

547
38:56.278 --> 38:59.514
You actually cooked that?

548
38:59.514 --> 39:01.910
Normally, I would've thrown the ingredients out,

549
39:01.910 --> 39:05.394
but strangely, I really wanted to try making what she gave me.

550
39:05.394 --> 39:09.258
Was it because it was the first time

551
39:09.258 --> 39:11.347
someone had prepared a meal for me?

552
39:13.270 --> 39:16.202
I thought things like soul food

553
39:16.202 --> 39:18.978
or Mom's cooking were all meaningless.

554
39:18.978 --> 39:20.962
But,

555
39:20.962 --> 39:25.570
I just didn't have anyone to share my feelings with.

556
39:33.378 --> 39:35.288
Can I ask you

557
39:36.410 --> 39:41.127
why did you disappear that day?

558
39:45.278 --> 39:47.066
Well...

559
39:50.266 --> 39:52.931
because you weren't there.

560
39:57.930 --> 40:00.298
It wasn't unexpected.

561
40:00.298 --> 40:02.857
As long as we had a good time, that's what counts.

562
40:06.354 --> 40:08.766
We missed each other.

563
40:08.766 --> 40:11.407
I went out to buy breakfast for us.

564
40:15.614 --> 40:17.538
It was my first time

565
40:18.510 --> 40:21.578
wanting to share my heart and eat breakfast

566
40:21.578 --> 40:24.520
with someone.

567
40:30.342 --> 40:32.553
Whenever I'm with you,

568
40:33.790 --> 40:36.741
I keep doing things I've never done before.

569
40:39.134 --> 40:42.647
I even get to know emotions I didn't know.

570
40:43.414 --> 40:46.067
I get the courage to try something... Oh!

571
40:52.397 --> 40:55.878
S-Sorry.

572
40:55.878 --> 40:59.762
I got a little dizzy...

573
40:59.762 --> 41:01.054
Just 30 seconds.

574
41:01.054 --> 41:04.602
No, just one minute...

575
41:23.826 --> 41:27.850
If you back down like that, you lose territory, right?

576
41:27.850 --> 41:29.934
I had to survive first.

577
41:29.934 --> 41:33.898
You survived, but there's no flavor in that play.

578
41:33.898 --> 41:36.784
Are you always so passive in your games?

579
41:39.074 --> 41:41.186
I'm a pacifist by nature, sir.

580
41:41.186 --> 41:43.098
That's why you only end up helping others.

581
41:43.098 --> 41:47.270
Because you dodged, the guy next to you took the prize, see?

582
41:48.109 --> 41:52.573
I lost. Still, I don't regret my move.

583
41:53.318 --> 41:54.990
- Come visit often. - Compared to me,

584
41:54.990 --> 41:58.406
playing with your friends would be much more fun.

585
41:58.406 --> 42:01.350
As you can see, my play style is pretty bland.

586
42:01.350 --> 42:03.181
It used to be.

587
42:03.181 --> 42:07.310
But they're all... gone.

588
42:07.310 --> 42:09.294
Gone where?

589
42:17.994 --> 42:20.028
- One more game? - Yes, sir!

590
42:49.146 --> 42:50.766
Sleep some more.

591
42:50.766 --> 42:53.444
I'll wake you up in an hour.

592
42:55.498 --> 43:01.719
Does this mean... we're doing it now?

593
43:06.874 --> 43:11.212
My underwear doesn't match today, so I can't...

594
43:15.230 --> 43:20.029
Just shoot me... Kill me now...

595
43:21.014 --> 43:22.782
My phone!

596
43:25.142 --> 43:27.005
Wait, what time is it?

597
43:28.726 --> 43:31.582
Oh, no! I'm so dead!

598
43:50.349 --> 43:51.866
I'm sorry.

599
43:51.866 --> 43:54.210
I should've woken you up, but I fell asleep too.

600
43:54.210 --> 43:57.870
No, it's fine. Go back to sleep. I have to rush home.

601
43:57.870 --> 44:01.053
I'll drive you.

602
44:08.142 --> 44:10.166
Man, what time is it?

603
44:14.590 --> 44:17.082
My arm...

604
44:17.082 --> 44:19.070
My whole body aches...

605
44:23.110 --> 44:24.978
Gosh...

606
44:27.714 --> 44:29.298
Ouch!

607
44:30.797 --> 44:31.798
You're up.

608
44:31.798 --> 44:33.406
You scared me!

609
44:33.406 --> 44:37.218
Have you been waiting up like this the whole time?

610
44:37.218 --> 44:40.858
What about Yeon Su?

611
44:40.858 --> 44:43.739
Seriously...

612
44:43.739 --> 44:47.818
Why would overtime last until this hour?

613
44:47.818 --> 44:53.397
Go inside and get some sleep. I'll wake you when she arrives.

614
44:54.650 --> 44:59.028
Children carve out their own paths,

615
44:59.666 --> 45:03.382
but I never expected her to cross the line so quietly.

616
45:05.954 --> 45:09.874
Maybe I've been holding onto her too tightly all this time.

617
45:09.874 --> 45:12.050
Why is that your fault?

618
45:12.050 --> 45:17.162
You know the Gongs. Once they fixate on something, they see it through.

619
45:17.162 --> 45:19.358
It's in the genes! In the genes!

620
45:19.358 --> 45:24.862
She's just faithfully carrying on our family tradition.

621
45:29.666 --> 45:33.142
By the way, doesn't his back hurt sleeping on the floor?

622
45:33.142 --> 45:35.474
Why is he still lying there instead of going home?

623
45:37.294 --> 45:41.578
How many bottles of makgeolli did they drink?

624
45:41.578 --> 45:44.673
Seriously, Dad...

625
45:50.926 --> 45:52.962
Hey! Gong Nam Su!

626
45:52.962 --> 45:54.210
Yeon Su!

627
45:54.210 --> 45:56.060
And... Mr. Dokgo?

628
45:56.698 --> 45:58.682
Are you just getting home now?

629
45:58.682 --> 46:00.090
Wait, did you two stay out all night together?

630
46:00.090 --> 46:01.951
- Overtime. - We fell asleep.

631
46:04.230 --> 46:06.630
Great timing!

632
46:06.630 --> 46:08.502
We fell asleep while working overtime.

633
46:08.502 --> 46:10.450
Still completely out of sync?

634
46:10.450 --> 46:12.134
Whatever, hurry and climb over.

635
46:12.134 --> 46:13.646
Me?

636
46:13.646 --> 46:14.910
Me?

637
46:17.774 --> 46:20.860
My leg is still throbbing...

638
46:24.098 --> 46:25.542
- Mr. Dokgo... - Huh?

639
46:25.542 --> 46:27.138
Hey, no way!

640
46:27.138 --> 46:30.398
- Could you hop over and open the gate? - Wait, hold on!

641
46:30.398 --> 46:32.070
You can go. We'll handle it ourselves.

642
46:32.070 --> 46:33.902
How can we handle it when both of us are limping?

643
46:33.902 --> 46:36.281
Mr. Dokgo, you're very tall!

644
46:36.281 --> 46:38.178
With your height, one hop is enough!

645
46:38.178 --> 46:42.715
Hey! How could you make the CEO jump the wall?

646
47:03.934 --> 47:09.362
Just push that wooden bar to the side!

647
47:09.362 --> 47:12.312
What are you doing

648
47:12.312 --> 47:16.266
jumping over our wall at this hour?

649
47:16.266 --> 47:18.092
Ma'am.

650
47:20.754 --> 47:22.730
Ah, I'm so dizzy...

651
47:25.918 --> 47:27.206
Godal!

652
47:27.206 --> 47:30.930
Yoon Jio, why are you here?

653
47:31.674 --> 47:33.658
Why are you up there?

654
47:33.658 --> 47:35.986
This won't work. Let me step on your back.

655
47:35.986 --> 47:37.826
Me?

656
47:58.558 --> 48:01.533
M-Mom...

657
48:01.533 --> 48:03.168
Ms. Gong!

658
48:04.138 --> 48:05.942
Mr. Yoon?

659
48:06.610 --> 48:08.351
Nam Su!

660
48:09.258 --> 48:11.762
Yeon Su, let's talk.

661
48:18.882 --> 48:20.655
Oh, no!

662
48:25.062 --> 48:28.530
Everyone... inside.

663
48:28.530 --> 48:32.126
Grab the popcorn!

664
48:41.358 --> 48:43.778
Explain yourselves.

665
48:43.778 --> 48:49.514
We just... finished work late, so Mr. Dokgo Dal gave me a ride home.

666
48:49.514 --> 48:53.210
I'll make this short. Which one is it?

667
48:53.210 --> 48:55.074
What?

668
48:56.450 --> 48:59.278
What do you mean, which one?

669
48:59.278 --> 49:00.550
Which of the two?

670
49:00.550 --> 49:03.250
Which... of whom?

671
49:03.250 --> 49:05.590
By the way, why did you sleep here?

672
49:05.590 --> 49:08.010
I drank makgeolli with her grandpa and passed out.

673
49:08.010 --> 49:10.354
Then why did you climb the wall?

674
49:10.354 --> 49:11.634
The gate was locked.

675
49:12.621 --> 49:15.701
I can't hear anything. Keep it down.

676
49:18.349 --> 49:20.049
[Encyclopedia of Pregnancy, Childbirth, and Childcare]

677
49:21.450 --> 49:23.086
What is... this?

678
49:23.086 --> 49:28.564
You tell me. There must be a reason you're reading it.

679
49:33.946 --> 49:36.071
You're pregnant!

680
49:36.794 --> 49:40.318
What? I'm... what?

681
49:40.318 --> 49:43.834
You punk, when did you?

682
49:46.746 --> 49:49.753
Mom! You don't actually think this is mine, do you?

683
49:49.753 --> 49:52.530
Tell me the truth. Which one is it?

684
49:53.806 --> 49:56.258
Yeon Su, just tell her! Number one or number two?

685
49:56.258 --> 49:58.102
- Hey, are you number two? - No way.

686
49:58.102 --> 50:00.229
- Never... absolutely not... - Wait, which number am I?

687
50:00.229 --> 50:02.190
Never! I swear it's not me, Mom!

688
50:02.190 --> 50:04.850
Then why was this book under your bed?

689
50:04.850 --> 50:06.262
What?

690
50:06.262 --> 50:11.190
This was under my bed?

691
50:14.806 --> 50:17.696
You jerk!

692
50:26.054 --> 50:28.630
Mom, just listen to me first.

693
50:28.630 --> 50:30.602
- Gong Yeon Su! - It's Gong Nam Su!

694
50:30.602 --> 50:32.754
It's not me! Gong Nam Su's girlfriend is pregnant!

695
50:32.754 --> 50:35.082
You traitor!

696
50:35.082 --> 50:37.230
You've disgraced our ancestors!

697
50:37.230 --> 50:39.965
You disgraced me, you little jerk!

698
50:39.965 --> 50:42.863
- What did you hide it under my bed? - Ms. Yeon Su!

699
50:43.618 --> 50:45.332
Unbelievable!

700
50:47.250 --> 50:49.895
Total chaos, the truth unfolds.

701
50:53.034 --> 50:54.594
Gong Nam Su... you...

702
50:54.594 --> 50:58.262
I'm sorry, Mom! It just happened!

703
50:58.262 --> 51:01.922
Oh, my!

704
51:01.922 --> 51:03.742
Good grief!

705
51:05.350 --> 51:08.254
Mom! She works at a sex toy company!

706
51:08.254 --> 51:11.362
And those two spent the night together!

707
51:11.362 --> 51:13.685
- Cut it out! - Is that true?

708
51:18.646 --> 51:20.960
Gong Yeon Su, answer me!

709
51:28.870 --> 51:30.686
I like her.

710
51:40.806 --> 51:45.075
I have feelings for Ms. Yeon Su.
